IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `tx-const-personal-taxes`

-- Texas Constitution art. VIII, ss 24-a, 24-b, 25, 26 -- the individual's questions, worked cases.
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law; expected values written from the text.

-- s 24-a: wages, a sole proprietor's profit, a partner's share, investment income, retirement income.
#ASSERT `Can Texas tax my income` `wages or salary` EQUALS `no: Texas may not tax the net incomes of individuals (Tex. Const. art. VIII, s 24-a)`
#ASSERT `Can Texas tax my income` `self-employment or business income as a sole proprietor` EQUALS `no: Texas may not tax the net incomes of individuals (Tex. Const. art. VIII, s 24-a)`
#ASSERT `Can Texas tax my income` `my share of partnership or unincorporated association income` EQUALS `no: Texas may not tax an individual's share of partnership or unincorporated association income (Tex. Const. art. VIII, s 24-a)`
#ASSERT `Can Texas tax my income` `retirement income or Social Security` EQUALS `no: Texas may not tax the net incomes of individuals (Tex. Const. art. VIII, s 24-a)`
#ASSERT (NOT `Must I file a Texas income tax return`)

-- s 24-b: a tax on my gain or on my sale is barred; property, sales and use taxes are left alone by (b).
#ASSERT (NOT (`May Texas impose this tax on my sale or gain` `a tax on my gain, realized or unrealized`))
#ASSERT (NOT (`May Texas impose this tax on my sale or gain` `a tax on selling or transferring a capital asset, payable by me as seller`))
#ASSERT `May Texas impose this tax on my sale or gain` `property tax (ad valorem)`
#ASSERT `May Texas impose this tax on my sale or gain` `sales tax or use tax on goods or services`

-- s 25.
#ASSERT (NOT `Can Texas tax my net worth`)

-- s 26.
#ASSERT `Can Texas tax an estate, inheritance or gift` `a tax on a dead person's estate because of the death` EQUALS `no (Tex. Const. art. VIII, s 26(a)(1))`
#ASSERT `Can Texas tax an estate, inheritance or gift` `a tax on my inheritance, legacy, succession or a gift to me` EQUALS `no, unless that tax was in effect on 1 January 2025, and then not at a higher rate or wider reach (Tex. Const. art. VIII, s 26(a)(2), (3))`
#ASSERT `Can Texas tax an estate, inheritance or gift` `a tax on a motor vehicle I am given` EQUALS `yes: s 26 does not prohibit it (Tex. Const. art. VIII, s 26(b))`
#ASSERT `Can Texas tax an estate, inheritance or gift` `property tax on what I inherit` EQUALS `yes: s 26 does not prohibit it (Tex. Const. art. VIII, s 26(b))`

-- The prohibitions: imposing the tax is a breach by the legislature.
#TRACE `s 24-a -- no individual income tax` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the legislature` DOES `impose a tax on the net incomes of individuals` AT 5
-- expect: BREACH BY the legislature, "Tex. Const. art. VIII, s 24-a: ..."
#TRACE `s 24-b -- no capital gains tax` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the legislature` DOES `impose a tax on an individual's capital gains` AT 5
-- expect: BREACH BY the legislature, "Tex. Const. art. VIII, s 24-b: ..."
#TRACE `s 25 -- no wealth tax` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the legislature` DOES `impose a tax based on wealth or net worth` AT 5
-- expect: BREACH BY the legislature, "Tex. Const. art. VIII, s 25: ..."
#TRACE `s 26 -- no death tax and no new transfer tax` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the legislature` DOES `impose a death tax, or a new or increased tax on an estate, inheritance or gift transfer` AT 5
-- expect: BREACH BY the legislature, "Tex. Const. art. VIII, s 26(a): ..."
-- And an unrelated act leaves the prohibition standing (no breach; a residual prohibition with no deadline).
#TRACE `s 24-a -- no individual income tax` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the legislature` DOES `impose a tax based on wealth or net worth` AT 5
-- expect: residual (the s 24-a prohibition still in force)
